    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\n`checkDigit` is now returned on the owner response as a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`. I followed the codebase's established pattern for response-only derived fields (`locality`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`, `initials`): a `@Transient` getter on the model, auto-mapped into the generated DTO by MapStruct, with the standalone algorithm factored into its own helper class (mirroring `CityRegion`/`RegionPostcodes`).\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n1. **`model/Luhn.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility helper: `Luhn.checkDigit(String)` computes the Luhn check digit over the decimal digits in a string, ignoring non-digits and null-safe.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getCheckDigit()` getter that delegates to `Luhn.checkDigit(customerCode)`, placed among the other derived getters.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` field (read-only integer 0\u20139) to the owner response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct populates it by name.\n\nNo changes were needed to the endpoint pipeline or mappers \u2014 `customerCode` is already assigned before the responder runs, and MapStruct maps the new field automatically by property name.\n\nThe `Owner` model stays thin (it just delegates), the Luhn algorithm lives in its own reusable unit, and no class absorbed unrelated logic. `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
